# Parmesan Minestrone

Based on [Chrissy Teigen Cravings Hungry for More](https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/553580/cravings-hungry-for-more-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250616010240/https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/553580/cravings-hungry-for-more-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman/)), pg. 50

{ rating="5" image="parmesan_minestrone.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 3 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1 large [yellow onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, cut into 1/2” dice
- [ ] 6 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } (3 tsp), diced
- [ ] 4 medium [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, halved and coined
- [ ] 2 [celery sticks]{ ing="celery-sticks" } or a green pepper, cut into 1/2” dice
- [ ] 3-4 cups vegetable or chicken broth. [Add more broth]{ ing="add-more-broth" } or water as needed
- [ ] 1 (28-oz) can of [diced tomatoes]{ ing="diced-tomatoes" } (keep juice) or ~1 lb (4-5 medium) fresh tomatoes (diced) with 1/2 tbsp of tomato paste
- [ ] 1 (15-oz) can [white beans]{ ing="white-beans" } (cannellini/navy, peruvian, pinto, etc.), drained and rinsed
- [ ] 1 (15-oz) can (keep juice), 1/2 bag of frozen, or fresh green beans (trimmed and cut into 1.5” pieces)
- [ ] 2 tsp [dried basil]{ ing="dried-basil" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" }
- [ ] 2/3 cup [pasta wheels]{ ing="pasta-wheels" } (~1/2 cup elbow/macaroni)
- [ ] 1 cup [Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese]{ ing="parmigiano-reggiano-cheese" }, plus more for garnish
- [ ] [Serve with baguette]{ ing="serve-with-baguette" } or toast

## Recipe

1. In a large ceramic dutch oven, heat the [oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } over medium heat. Add [onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" } and cook ~8 min until tender. Add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } and cook 1 additional minute
1. Add the [carrots]{ ing="carrots" } and celery and cook ~4 min until slightly softened
1. Add the [broth]{ ing="add-more-broth" }, the three canned ingredients, and spices. Bring to a boil then reduce to a simmer and cook for 20 min until thickened
1. Add the pasta and cook until tender for another ~10 min
1. Stir in the Parmesan and season with additional [salt]{ ing="salt" } and [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }.

## Notes

- [If using dry beans, see no-soak recipe](../sides/no_soak_instant_pot_beans.html)
